problem:
Find all integer pairs \((x, y)\) that satisfy the equation \(2x^2 + y^2 + 8x - 2y + 10 = 0\). ^{
Solution:
Rewrite the equation in vertex form and solve for integer solutions.

Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the following system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 3 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 7 \pmod{11} \\
x \equiv 9 \pmod{13}
\end{cases}
\]

求解下列同余方程组：
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 2 \pmod{3} \\
x \equiv 3 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 4 \pmod{7}
\end{cases}
\]
